ion\n- **Architectural strategy** — Mobile Redesign Architect Lead, defined architectural standards\n\n### Behavioral/Culture Match\n\n- **Technical leadership** — posting emphasizes \"thought leader and technical anchor,\" aligns with candidate's strength in mentoring and process standardization\n- **AI in engineering workflows** — candidate actively uses AI tooling (Claude Code) in freelance work\n- **Process standardization** — \"best-practice-by-default\" philosophy at PNC directly matches\n- **Autonomous work style** — candidate thrives in autonomous roles\n\n### Salary Benchmark\n\n- **Posted range:** $127,050 - $181,500/year\n- **Floor:** $150k+ for remote/remote-friendly roles\n- **Analysis:** The top end ($181k) clears the $150k floor, but the base starts well below. Principal level should command the top of the range. Colorado cost of living is lower than Pittsburgh, so $181k in Englewood CO roughly equals $190k+ in Pittsburgh PPP.\n\n### Deal-Breakers & Concerns\n\n- **📍 Englewood, CO requires relocation** — not remote, not nearby, requires full relocation\n- **⚠ People management signals** — posting uses \"thought leader and technical anchor\" and \"drives outward-facing integration projects.\" However, these are NOT people management terms — they describe technical influence. The role does NOT mention \"direct reports,\" \"people manager,\" or \"engineering manager.\" This is an Individual Contributor role.\n- **Android TV niche** — specialized form factor far from core mobile app experience, but the underlying Android skills transfer\n- **Telecommunications sector** — not in target sectors (FinTech, Tech/Platforms, modernization), but EchoStar is undergoing modernization (streaming, smart home)\n\n### Overall Fit Score: 72 — Good Fit\n\n**Recommendation: Strong candidate despite relocation requirement.**\n\nThe technical alignment is excellent — Kotlin/Compose, modular architecture, CI/CD, observability, and AI workflows all match. The Principal title 