                  "output": "---\nframework_version: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# Candidate Profile\n\n## Identity\n- **Name:** Franco N. Colaizzi\n- **Location:** Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania\n- **Languages:** English\n- **CV language:** English\n- **Status:** Freelance Developer\n- **LinkedIn headline:** \"Principal Android Software Engineer\"\n- **LinkedIn:** linkedin.com/in/fnc314\n- **GitHub:** github.com/fnc314\n- **Portfolio:** www.fnc314.dev | blog.fnc314.dev\n- **Email:** fnc314@gmail.com\n- **Phone:** 412-721-9550\n\n## Education\n- **Web Development Immersive** (Jan 2014 - April 2014) - General Assembly (San Francisco, CA)\n- **Bachelor of Science, Mathematics** (2011) - University of Pittsburgh (Pittsburgh, PA)\n\n## Professional Experience\n\n### Freelance Developer (01/2026 - Present) - Independent | Pittsburgh, PA, USA\n- Spearheaded development of a location-based dating app using React Native (Expo), Firebase, and Google Cloud Platform, effectively contributing to full-stack and backend systems.\n- Leveraged generative AI tooling within VS Code to accelerate independent feature prototyping, while retaining strict output validation.\n- Authored the technical engineering series \"Taming the Elephant Herd\" at blog.fnc314.dev, publishing deep-dives on Gradle build optimization, repository maintenance, and developer experience.\n\n### Director, Consulting Expert (08/2014 - 01/2026) - CGI | Pittsburgh, PA, USA\n- Served as a technical expert, mentoring peer engineers and defining architectural strategy for enterprise applications across clients including PNC Financial Services, PPG Industries, and Samsung Electronics. Founded the CGI I.T. Girl Challenge, authoring foundational documentation and onboarding community partners including Pittsburgh Public Schools.\n\n#### Android Mobile Project Tech Lead (01/2020 - 06/2025) - PNC Financial Services (Client)\n- Lead Architect for the flagship Android app (3.5M+ MAU), designing the mobile-to-backend interface for a highly resilient, high-volume in-app payment processing platform.\n- Modularized the entire codebase from a single \"god-module\" into a properly organized multi-module repository, reducing build times by 70% and isolating code contributions thereby reducing conflicts in merges.\n- Automated credential setup and environment validation with custom Bash scripts, reducing developer onboarding time by 80%.\n- Set technical standards and drove adoption across teams, breaking down complex initiatives into executable phases.\n- Drove the implementation of in-app card payment acceptance integrating with a paired Bluetooth (BLE) card-reader device and third-party SDK.\n- Produced comprehensive technical documentation to facilitate knowledge sharing and maintain feature parity.\n- Partnered with Product and UX leadership to define roadmaps, aligning high-impact technical debt reduction with business value for stakeholders.\n\n#### Mobile Redesign Architect Lead (11/2023 - 06/2025) - PNC Financial Services (Client)\n- Led major architectural transformations, instituting a 'best-practice-by-default' philosophy to seamlessly bridge Android and backend systems.\n- Coordinated cross-platform Design System governance, eliminating hardcoded UI values by mandating 100% semantic token adoption.\n- Engineered a Gradle module-generation workflow to enforce project-wide naming conventions and prevent architectural drift.\n- Created a centralized workflow with enforced PR restrictions and direct integration with string management platforms (GL Strings/Applanga).\n- Crafted interactive Bash scripts to streamline feature contributions and empower teams to build independently.\n- Accelerated development by enforcing a design token system, launching dynamic screen sizes, dark mode, and branded themes without increasing project scope.\n\n#### Android Security & Authentication Tech Lead (08/2019 - 01/2020) - PNC Financial Services (Client)\n- Engineered a modern authentication platform, migrating 10M+ active users with zero downtime.\n- Pioneered a Version Catalog (.toml) and KTS migration, creating a fully type-safe, auditable Gradle build system.\n- Secured 98% of mobile fraud avenues and streamlined security integrations to enable rapid team adoption.\n- Designed observability patterns to pinpoint trouble spots in user flows and streamline issue reproduction.\n\n#### Web Development Lead (08/2017 - 08/2019) - PNC Financial Services (Client)\n- Guided the growth and development of peer engineers with mentoring and coaching across a 25+ person organization, delivering high-impact, scalable solutions during the redesign of a large-scale enterprise platform.\n\n#### Web Developer (08/2016 - 08/2017) - PNC Financial Services (Client)\n- Partnered closely with product owners and designers to architect and deliver the administration portal supporting the launch of the Zelle peer-to-peer payment platform.\n\n#### Web Developer (01/2015 - 08/2016) - PPG Industries (Client)\n- Reduced deployment time for brand-specific white-label applications from days to hours by streamlining deployment processes and enhancing automation tools.\n\n#### Android Developer (01/2015 - 08/2016) - Samsung (Client)\n- Designed solutions for complex, cross-system initiatives, delivering an Android FIDO authenticator proof-of-concept that spring-boarded institutional adoption of Samsung Knox and MFA.\n\n## Technical Skills\n- **Programming Languages:** Kotlin | Java | JavaScript/TypeScript | Bash\n- **Frameworks & Libraries:** Android | Kotlin Multiplatform | Jetpack Compose | Coroutines/Flow | MVI | Clean Architecture | Use Cases/Interactors\n- **Build & DevOps:** Gradle (KTS/Groovy) | CI/CD | Jenkins | GitHub Actions | DevEx\n- **Cloud & Backend:** Firebase | Google Cloud | Glassbox | Split.io | Akamai\n- **Platforms & Security:** Samsung Knox | FIDO | MFA | Mobile Payment Systems\n- **Testing & Automation:** A/B Testing | Bash Scripting | Fastlane\n- **Core Competencies:** Mobile/Web Applications, Software Architecture, API Standards, Stakeholder Alignment, Accessibility.\n- **Explicit Grounding Guardrails:** Not an iOS/Swift developer (no production Swift authoring; surface familiarity only). Enterprise career at PNC was strictly human-driven engineering without AI tooling; AI tool usage is restricted to IDE-assisted independent feature prototyping in Freelance work.\n\n## Publications & Authorship\n- **\"Taming the Elephant Herd\"** - blog.fnc314.dev (Deep-dives on Gradle build optimization, repository maintenance, and developer experience)."
