1} 08/2017 - 08/2019}\\\\\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PNC Financial Services (Client)} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PITTSBURGH, PENNSYLVANIA}\\vspace{2pt}\\\\\n{\\itshape\\sffamily Guided the growth and development of peer engineers with mentoring and coaching across a 25+ person organization, delivering high-impact, scalable solutions during the redesign of a large-scale enterprise platform.}\n}\n\n% --- PNC Zelle ---\n\\item{\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\normalsize Web Developer} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\normalsize\\color{color1} 08/2016 - 08/2017}\\\\\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PNC Financial Services (Client)} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PITTSBURGH, PENNSYLVANIA}\\vspace{2pt}\\\\\n{\\itshape\\sffamily Partnered closely with product owners and designers to architect and deliver the administration portal supporting the launch of the Zelle peer-to-peer payment platform.}\n}\n\n% --- PPG ---\n\\item{\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\normalsize Web Developer} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\normalsize\\color{color1} 01/2015 - 08/2016}\\\\\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PPG Industries (Client)} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PITTSBURGH, PENNSYLVANIA}\\vspace{2pt}\\\\\n{\\itshape\\sffamily Reduced deployment time for brand-specific white-label applications from days to hours by streamlining deployment processes and enhancing automation tools.}\n}\n\n% --- Samsung PoC ---\n\\item{\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\normalsize Android Developer} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\normalsize\\color{color1} 01/2015 - 08/2016}\\\\\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} Samsung (Client)} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\small\\color{color1} PITTSBURGH, PENNSYLVANIA}\\vspace{2pt}\\\\\n{\\itshape\\sffamily Designed solutions for complex, cross-system initiatives, delivering an Android FIDO authenticator proof-of-concept that spring-boarded institutional adoption of Samsung Knox and MFA.}\n}\n\n\\end{itemize}\n\n% ============================================================\n%     EDUCATION\n% ============================================================\n\\section{EDUCATION}\n\\vspace{1pt}\n\\begin{itemize}[label={}, leftmargin=0pt, itemsep=5pt]\n\\item{\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\large\\color{color1} Web Development Immersive} {\\sffamily | General Assembly | San Francisco, CA} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\large\\color{color1} 2014}\n}\n\\item{\n\\textbf{\\ttfamily\\large\\color{color1} Bachelor of Science, Mathematics} {\\sffamily | University of Pittsburgh | Pittsburgh, PA} \\hfill \\textbf{\\ttfamily\\large\\color{color1} 2011}\n}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}\n</CV_DRAFT>\n\n<COVER_LETTER_DRAFT file=\"job-applications/echostar/principal-android-engineer/2026-11-12/cover_echostar_principal_android_engineer.tex\">\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n% Cover Letter - EchoStar Corporation, Principal Android Engineer\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\n\\documentclass[]{cover}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage[normalem]{ulem}\n\\newcommand{\\myhref}[2]{\\href{#1}{\\uline{#2}}}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\n\\rfoot{Page \\thepage \\hspace{0pt}}\n\\thispagestyle{empty}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\begin{document}\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%     TITLE NAME\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\\namesection{}{\\Huge{Franco N. Colaizzi}}{  \\myhref{mailto:fnc314@gmail.com}{fnc314@gmail.com} | 412-721-9550 | \\urlstyle{same}\\myhref{https://www.fnc314.dev}{www.fnc314.dev} | \\urlstyle{same}\\myhref{https://blog.fnc314.dev}{blog.fnc314.dev} | \\urlstyle{same}\\myhref{https://linkedin.com/in/fnc314}{linkedin.com/in/fnc314}\n}\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%     MAIN COVER LETTER CONTENT\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\n\\currentdate{\\today}\n\\lettercontent{Dear EchoStar and DISH Technology Hiring Team,}\n\n\\lettercontent{I am applying for the Principal Android Engineer position at EchoStar. EchoStar's mission to advance connectivity and video delivery across diverse customer device fleets, spanning DISH TV, Sling TV, and Boost Mobile, requires uncompromising playback stability, modular application frameworks that decouple development teams, and deep observability across distributed hardware. Backed by 10+ years of technical leadership defining enterprise Android architecture for platforms serving 3.5M+ active users, I bring the architectural discipline needed to anchor your platform initiatives.}\n\n\\lettercontent{Throughout my career leading flagship Android architectures and mentoring 25+ engineers, I have treated system modularization, deterministic contracts, and telemetry instrumentation as core engineering foundations. Guided by a B.S. in Mathematics and production expertise in Kotlin, Coroutines, Jetpack Compose, and platform-level integrations, I offer direct experience addressing EchoStar's technical priorities:}\n\n{\\raggedright\\fontspec[Path = OpenFonts/fonts/raleway/]{Raleway-Medium}\\fontsize{11pt}{13pt}\\selectfont\n\\begin{itemize}\n    \\item \\textbf{Modular Architecture \\& Codebase Scalability:} Decomposed a monolithic enterprise Android codebase (3.5M+ MAU) from a single ``god-module'' into an organized multi-module repository, cutting build times by 70\\% and instituting automated module-generation workflows to enforce architectural boundaries.\n    \\item \\textbf{System Observability \\& Fleet Telemetry:} Designed custom observability patterns and telemetry instrumentation to isolate bottlenecks in complex user flows, reduce issue reproduction time, and safeguard mission-critical mobile-to-backend interfaces against field regressions.\n    \\item \\textbf{Platform-Level Integrations \\& Hardware Coordination:} Engineered resilient peripheral communication integrating paired Bluetooth (BLE) hardware with custom SDKs, and authored an Android FIDO authenticator proof-of-concept that established institutional adoption of Samsung Knox and MFA.\n    \\item \\textbf{Engineering Standards, DevEx \\& AI Workflows:} Instituted a ``best-practice-by-default'' philosophy, automated credential setups reducing onboarding time by 80\\%, published the technical series \\myhref{https://blog.fnc314.dev}{\\textit{\"Taming the Elephant Herd\"}} on build optimization, and integrated Claude Code into independent prototyping workflows with rigorous validation gates.\n\\end{itemize}\\par}\n\\vspace{6pt}\n\n\\lettercontent{While my enterprise production work centered on high-volume financial platforms and connected peripherals rather than dedicated set-top box or Android TV media engines, the core engineering imperatives are identical: strict lifecycle discipline, low-latency streaming interfaces, resilient error handling, and robust telemetry across distributed hardware fleets. I welcome the opportunity to participate in a technical assessment or whiteboarding session and discuss how my platform background aligns with EchoStar's streaming reliability and connectivity goals.}\n\n\\begin{flushright}\n\\closing{Kind regards,}\n\n\\signature{Franco N. Colaizzi}\n\\end{flushright}\n\\end{document}\n</COVER_LETTER_DRAFT>\n\n### 5. Job Posting\n<JOB_POSTING>\n# EchoStar Corporation — Principal Android Engineer\nLocation: Englewood, CO (Onsite)\nDepartment: DISH Technology\nSalary Range: $127,050.00/Year - $181,500.00/Year\n\nCandidates must be willing to participate in at least one in-person interview, which may include a live whiteboarding or technical assessment session.\n\nEnterprise Android deployments require robust architecture, reliable playback, and enterprise-grade observability across diverse device fleets. The Principal Android Engineer solves critical scale and stability challenges across the full Android stack, from low-level media playback engines to modular application frameworks. As a thought leader and technical anchor, this role not only shapes the internal architecture but also drives outward-facing integration projects and aligns engineering deliverables with overarching business goals. This position establishes technical roadmaps, sets engineering standards, and optimizes release pipelines for mission-critical customer software. By integrating modern Android architectures and AI-assisted engineering workflows, the role ensures operational reliability and continuous system performance across all deployed hardware.\n\nKey Objectives:\n• Act as the technical anchor for the business, translating overarching company objectives into actionable engineering strategies that drive platform growth and market success.\n• Spearhead high-stakes, outward-facing integration projects collaborating directly with original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), silicon vendors, and key B2B integration partners.\n• Act as a thought leader and primary technical authority for the broader engineering organization, driving architectural alignment across product, backend, and external partner teams.\n• Lead the technical architecture and long-term roadmap of the enterprise Android application, modularizing the codebase to support rapid feature deployment and system scalability.\n• Establish a core observability foundation—including real-time metrics, logging, crash telemetry, and field analytics—to improve application reliability across all deployed customer devices.\n• Drive media playback performance and streaming reliability across the fleet using advanced frameworks, digital rights management, and adaptive protocols.\n• Integrate AI-assisted development tools and automated workflows into the engineering lifecycle to increase team throughput and elevate code quality standards.\n\nCore Skills and Competencies:\n• Demonstrated thought leadership with the ability to act as the definitive technical escalation point (anchor), capable of driving organizational change and presenting architectural vision to executive stakeholders.\n• Strong commercial awareness and the ability to drive business outcomes by balancing technical perfection with speed-to-market, complex external integration requirements, and ROI.\n• Deep expertise in modern Android development standards, including Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, coroutines, and scalable architectural patterns.\n• Proven critical experience leading production-scale media playback architectures utilizing ExoPlayer/Media3, adaptive streaming protocols (HLS/DASH), and digital rights management.\n• Proficiency in AI application within software engineering workflows to optimize code review processes, automated testing, and development efficiency.\n• Demonstrated competency in high-scale Android application quality management, including continuous integration, automated testing strategies, and field telemetry analysis.\n\nAdditional Qualifications:\n• Experience with Android TV, embedded Android, or set-top box form factors\n• Experience with live television, streaming video, or low-latency media applications\n• Experience working with original equipment manufacturers, silicon vendors, or platform integration partners\n\nMinimum Requirements:\n• Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience)\n• 10+ years of professional software engineering experience, including significant experience as a technical lead on Android applications\n• Required: Kotlin, Jetpack, and modern Android architectural frameworks; Media playback frameworks (ExoPlayer or Media3) and streaming protocols; System observability, automated CI/CD pipelines, and enterprise application lifecycle management.\n\nAbout Our Department:\nOur DISH Technology team challenges the status quo and reimagines capabilities across industries. Connecting consumers with products and platforms of tomorrow.\n\nAbout Our Company:\nEchoStar is reimagining the future of connectivity. Brands include Boost Mobile, DISH TV, Gen Mobile, Hughes, and Sling TV.\n</JOB_POSTING>\n\n### 6. Produce Feedback\n\nReturn your feedback in **two parts**:\n\n**Part A — Structured edits (preferred format whenever possible):**\nA JSON array of concrete edits the drafter can apply directly without re-reading the files. Each edit is an object:\n```json\n{\n  \"file\": \"job-applications/echostar/principal-android-engineer/2026-11-12/main_echostar_principal_android_engineer.tex\" | \"job-applications/echostar/principal-android-engineer/2026-11-12/cover_echostar_principal_android_engineer.tex\",\n  \"old_string\": \"<exact text currently in the draft>\",\n  \"new_string\": \"<replacement text>\",\n  \"reason\": \"<one-line rationale: keyword match / company angle / reframing / style / grounding>\"\n}\n```\nOnly use this format when you can quote the exact `old_string` from the drafts above. Make `old_string` unique — include enough surrounding context so it matches exactly once per file.\n\n**Part B — Narrative suggestions (for judgment calls that are not mechanical edits):**\nProse suggestions grouped by category. Produce each category even if your finding is \"no issues\" — silence on a category can be mistaken for skipping it.\n- **Missed keywords/requirements**\n- **Company/department-specific angles**\n- **Action-oriented reframing**\n- **Tone and style issues**\n\nCRITICAL RULE: All suggestions must be grounded in actual profile data. Do NOT suggest fabricating skills, experience, or achievements. If a requirement is a gap, say so honestly and suggest how to frame adjacent experience instead.\n\nDo not run a verification checklist — the drafter will do that in the final step. Focus on content critique.\n\nReturn Part A and Part B together as a single structured message.\n"
